ihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     URL path `/notes/<int:note_id>/delete` (notes.py:41)\n+Sink:       routes/notes.py:48 — `session.delete(note)` with no `note.user_id == current_user.id` check\n+\n+```python\n+def delete_note(note_id: int):\n+    with Session() as session:\n+        note = session.get(Note, note_id)\n+        if note is None:\n+            flash('Note not found', 'warning')\n+        else:\n+            session.delete(note)   # line 48 — no ownership check\n+            session.commit()\n+```\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Log in, POST to `/notes/2/delete` where note 2 belongs to another user → 2. `session.get(Note, 2)` returns the note; no ownership check → 3. another user's note is deleted (data destruction).\n+**Mitigations:** Partial — listing (`get_notes_for_user`) filters by user_id, but the delete endpoint does not.\n+**Fix:** Add `if note.user_id != current_user.id and not current_user.is_admin: abort(403)` before deletion.\n+\n ### app.py:11 — Hardcoded Flask secret_key (session forgery)\n **CWE:** CWE-798\n **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n **Impact:** HIGH\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","patch":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -226,8 +226,35 @@\n **Exploit:** 1. Submit signup with `registration_code = \"' OR '1'='1\"` → 2. WHERE becomes `WHERE code = '' OR '1'='1'` → matches a row → token consumed → user created; or UNION-based extraction → 3. invite-code gate bypassed (unauthenticated signup) and/or data exfiltrati