{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788193237292,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_3e8876ae","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","oldString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the hardcoded key (present in source / public repo) → 2. Forges a signed Flask session cookie (e.g. `user_id=1` for admin) → 3. `user_loader` resolves the id → authenticated as admin (auth bypass).\n**Mitigations:** None (key is static and weak).\n**Fix:** Load `SECRET_KEY` from an environment variable / secret manager; use a strong random value, never hardcode it.","newString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the hardcoded key (present in source / public repo) → 2. Forges a signed Flask session cookie (e.g. `user_id=1` for admin) → 3. `user_loader` resolves the id → authenticated as admin (auth bypass).\n**Mitigations:** None (key is static and weak).\n**Fix:** Load `SECRET_KEY` from an environment variable / secret manager; use a strong random value, never hardcode it.\n\n### db_seed.py:17-19 — Hardcoded admin credentials (weak password)\n**CWE:** CWE-259\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** HIGH\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood HIGH = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSink:       db_seed.py:18-19 — admin account `admin@evfa.com` seeded with plaintext `b'admin'` (bcrypt-hashed at rest, but the value is hardcoded in source)\n\n```python\nadmin = User('admin@evfa.com',\n             hashpw(b'admin', gensalt()).decode(), True)\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. `setup_db()` (app.py:21) runs on every start and creates `admin@evfa.com`/`admin` on a fresh DB → 2. the plaintext password `admin` is hardcoded in the seed script and documented in the README → 3. attacker logs in as admin and reaches the admin-only /registration-codes route.\n**Mitigations:** Password is bcrypt-hashed in the DB, but the value is trivially guessable and hardcoded.\n**Fix:** Do not seed privileged accounts with weak, hardcoded passwords; require password setup on first run, or use strong randomly-generated seed values kept out of source control.\n\n### db_seed.py:9 — Hardcoded static registration code\n**CWE:** CWE-798\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSink:       db_seed.py:9 — `static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'` (also published in README)\n\n```python\nstatic_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'\nsession.add(RegistrationCode(static_code))\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the well-known code (hardcoded + in README) → 2. Uses it at /signup to bypass the invite-generation process → 3. creates a (normal) user account without an admin-issued code.\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Generate the static code at deploy time (env/secret) rather than hardcoding it; do not publish it in documentation."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -271,4 +271,44 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the hardcoded key (present in source / public repo) → 2. Forges a signed Flask session cookie (e.g. `user_id=1` for admin) → 3. `user_loader` resolves the id → authenticated as admin (auth bypass).\n **Mitigations:** None (key is static and weak).\n **Fix:** Load `SECRET_KEY` from an environment variable / secret manager; use a strong random value, never hardcode it.\n+\n+### db_seed.py:17-19 — Hardcoded admin credentials (weak password)\n+**CWE:** CWE-259\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** HIGH\n+**Likelihood:** HIGH\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood HIGH = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Sink:       db_seed.py:18-19 — admin account `admin@evfa.com` seeded with plaintext `b'admin'` (bcrypt-hashed at rest, but the value is hardcoded in source)\n+\n+```python\n+admin = User('admin@evfa.com',\n+             hashpw(b'admin', gensalt()).decode(), True)\n+```\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. `setup_db()` (app.py:21) runs on every start and creates `admin@evfa.com`/`admin` on a fresh DB → 2. the plaintext password `admin` is hardcoded in the seed script and documented in the README → 3. attacker logs in as admin and reaches the admin-only /registration-codes route.\n+**Mitigations:** Password is bcrypt-hashed in the DB, but the value is trivially guessable and hardcoded.\n+**Fix:** Do not seed privileged accounts with weak, hardcoded passwords; require password setup on first run, or use strong randomly-generated seed values kept out of source control.\n+\n+### db_seed.py:9 — Hardcoded static registration code\n+**CWE:** CWE-798\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** LOW\n+**Likelihood:** HIGH\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Sink:       db_seed.py:9 — `static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'` (also published in README)\n+\n+```python\n+static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'\n+session.add(RegistrationCode(static_code))\n+```\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the well-known code (hardcoded + in README) → 2. Uses it at /signup to bypass the invite-generation process → 3. creates a (normal) user account without an admin-issued code.\n+**Mitigations:** None.\n+**Fix:** Generate the static code at deploy time (env/secret) rather than hardcoding it; do not publish it in documentation.\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","patch":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -271,4 +271,44 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the hardcoded key (present in source / public repo) → 2. Forges a signed Flask session cookie (e.g. `user_id=1` for admin) → 3. `user_loader` resolves the id → authenticated as admin (auth bypass).\n **Mitigations:** None (key is static and weak).\n **Fix:** Load `SECRET_KEY` from an environment variable / secret manager; use a strong random value, never hardcode it.\n+\n+### db_seed.py:17-19 — Hardcoded admin credentials (weak password)\n+**CWE:** CWE-259\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** HIGH\n+**Likelihood:** HIGH\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood HIGH = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Sink:       db_seed.py:18-19 — admin account `admin@evfa.com` seeded with plaintext `b'admin'` (bcrypt-hashed at rest, but the value is hardcoded in source)\n+\n+```python\n+admin = User('admin@evfa.com',\n+             hashpw(b'admin', gensalt()).decode(), True)\n+```\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. `setup_db()` (app.py:21) runs on every start and creates `admin@evfa.com`/`admin` on a fresh DB → 2. the plaintext password `admin` is hardcoded in the seed script and documented in the README → 3. attacker logs in as admin and reaches the admin-only /registration-codes route.\n+**Mitigations:** Password is bcrypt-hashed in the DB, but the value is trivially guessable and hardcoded.\n+**Fix:** Do not seed privileged accounts with weak, hardcoded passwords; require password setup on first run, or use strong randomly-generated seed values kept out of source control.\n+\n+### db_seed.py:9 — Hardcoded static registration code\n+**CWE:** CWE-798\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** LOW\n+**Likelihood:** HIGH\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Sink:       db_seed.py:9 — `static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'` (also published in README)\n+\n+```python\n+static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'\n+session.add(RegistrationCode(static_code))\n+```\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the well-known code (hardcoded + in README) → 2. Uses it at /signup to bypass the invite-generation process → 3. creates a (normal) user account without an admin-issued code.\n+**Mitigations:** None.\n+**Fix:** Generate the static code at deploy time (env/secret) rather than hardcoding it; do not publish it in documentation.\n","additions":40,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":".security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","time":{"start":1788193237284,"end":1788193237289}},"id":"prt_0589f690d001s2Wd40GJpdu0Uj","sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","messageID":"msg_0589ea681001ze77yfe21yALP0"}}
