{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788193455978,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_07ba0cb5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","oldString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the well-known code (hardcoded + in README) → 2. Uses it at /signup to bypass the invite-generation process → 3. creates a (normal) user account without an admin-issued code.\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Generate the static code at deploy time (env/secret) rather than hardcoding it; do not publish it in documentation.","newString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the well-known code (hardcoded + in README) → 2. Uses it at /signup to bypass the invite-generation process → 3. creates a (normal) user account without an admin-issued code.\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Generate the static code at deploy time (env/secret) rather than hardcoding it; do not publish it in documentation.\n\n### utils/profile_image.py:6-8 — SSRF via unvalidated `urlopen` (profile image URL)\n**CWE:** CWE-918\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** MODERATE\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     forms/account_form.py profile_image field → `form.profile_image.data` (account.py:87)\nTransform:  account.py:87 → `get_base64_image_blob(...)` → `download(url)`\nSink:       utils/profile_image.py:7 — `urlopen(url)` (unvalidated, user-controlled)\n\n```python\ndef download(url: str) -> bytes:\n    with urlopen(url) as response:\n        return response.read()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. On /account, set profile_image to `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` (cloud metadata) or an internal endpoint → 2. server-side `urlopen` fetches it → 3. the returned bytes are base64-encoded into the response → cloud credentials / internal data exfiltrated.\n**Mitigations:** Partial — `guess_type(url)` guesses a mimetype from the string only; it does not validate the response content-type or the URL scheme/host, so it does not actually prevent SSRF.\n**Fix:** Allowlist scheme (https only), block private/link-local/metadata IP ranges, and verify the fetched bytes are a real image (content-type / magic bytes)."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -311,4 +311,27 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the well-known code (hardcoded + in README) → 2. Uses it at /signup to bypass the invite-generation process → 3. creates a (normal) user account without an admin-issued code.\n **Mitigations:** None.\n **Fix:** Generate the static code at deploy time (env/secret) rather than hardcoding it; do not publish it in documentation.\n+\n+### utils/profile_image.py:6-8 — SSRF via unvalidated `urlopen` (profile image URL)\n+**CWE:** CWE-918\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** MODERATE\n+**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     forms/account_form.py profile_image field → `form.profile_image.data` (account.py:87)\n+Transform:  account.py:87 → `get_base64_image_blob(...)` → `download(url)`\n+Sink:       utils/profile_image.py:7 — `urlopen(url)` (unvalidated, user-controlled)\n+\n+```python\n+def download(url: str) -> bytes:\n+    with urlopen(url) as response:\n+        return response.read()\n+```\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. On /account, se