{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788193590354,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_8f923dba","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","oldString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker exploits any web vuln (SSTI/pickle/SQLi) → 2. code execution as root inside the container → 3. full container compromise / host pivot (no user boundary).\n**Mitigations:** None — no `USER` directive; `www-data` is only applied to copied files.\n**Fix:** Add `USER www-data` (or a dedicated non-root user) before the `CMD`, and drop `build-essential`/`python3-dev` from the runtime image.","newString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker exploits any web vuln (SSTI/pickle/SQLi) → 2. code execution as root inside the container → 3. full container compromise / host pivot (no user boundary).\n**Mitigations:** None — no `USER` directive; `www-data` is only applied to copied files.\n**Fix:** Add `USER www-data` (or a dedicated non-root user) before the `CMD`, and drop `build-essential`/`python3-dev` from the runtime image.\n\n### docker-compose.yml — no resource limits, restart policy, or hardening\n**CWE:** CWE-400 (resource limits)\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** LOW\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `docker-compose.yml` lines 3-7 (build + `ports: - 5000:80`).\nTransform:  No `deploy.resources.limits`, no `restart:` policy, no `security_opt` (seccomp/apparmor).\nSink:       Service `extremely_vulnerable_flask_app` — unbounded container resources, no auto-restart, no syscall filtering.\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`)."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -356,4 +356,21 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker exploits any web vuln (SSTI/pickle/SQLi) → 2. code execution as root inside the container → 3. full container compromise / host pivot (no user boundary).\n **Mitigations:** None — no `USER` directive; `www-data` is only applied to copied files.\n **Fix:** Add `USER www-data` (or a dedicated non-root user) before the `CMD`, and drop `build-essential`/`python3-dev` from the runtime image.\n+\n+### docker-compose.yml — no resource limits, restart policy, or hardening\n+**CWE:** CWE-400 (resource limits)\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** LOW\n+**Likelihood:** LOW\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     `docker-compose.yml` lines 3-7 (build + `ports: - 5000:80`).\n+Transform:  No `deploy.resources.limits`, no `restart:` policy, no `security_opt` (seccomp/apparmor).\n+Sink:       Service `extremely_vulnerable_flask_app` — unbounded container resources, no auto-restart, no syscall filtering.\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n+**Mitigations:** None.\n+**Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`).\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","patch":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -356,4 +356,21 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker exploits any web vuln (SSTI/pickle/SQLi) → 2. code execution as root inside the container → 3. full container compromise / host pivot (no user boundary).\n **Mitigations:** None — no `USER` directive; `www-data` is only applied to copied files.\n **Fix:** Add `USER www-data` (or a dedicated non-root user) before the `CMD`, and drop `build-essential`/`python3-dev` from the runtime image.\n+\n+### docker-compose.yml — no resource limits, restart policy, or hardening\n+**CWE:** CWE-400 (resource limits)\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** LOW\n+**Likelihood:** LOW\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     `docker-compose.yml` lines 3-7 (build + `ports: - 5000:80`).\n+Transform:  No `deploy.resources.limits`, no `restart:` policy, no `security_opt` (seccomp/apparmor).\n+Sink:       Service `extremely_vulnerable_flask_app` — unbounded container resources, no auto-restart, no syscall filtering.\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n+**Mitigations:** None.\n+**Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`).\n","additions":17,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":".security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","time":{"start":1788193590347,"end":1788193590351}},"id":"prt_058a4cc2e001i2qZS5DJUkzhCQ","sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","messageID":"msg_058a475b0001PPpUOjJYrFW87F"}}
