{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788193626016,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_ace6b9eb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","oldString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`).","newString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`).\n\n### uwsgi.ini — no request timeout (worker-exhaustion DoS)\n**CWE:** CWE-400\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** LOW\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `uwsgi.ini` line 6 (`processes = 5`), no `--harakiri`/`--request-timeout`.\nTransform:  A slow `urlopen` (profile_image SSRF, utils/profile_image.py:7) blocks one worker indefinitely; with only 5 workers, 5 slow requests exhaust all.\nSink:       uwsgi rejects further requests (503) — DoS.\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n**Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n**Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`)."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -373,4 +373,21 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n **Mitigations:** None.\n **Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`).\n+\n+### uwsgi.ini — no request timeout (worker-exhaustion DoS)\n+**CWE:** CWE-400\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** LOW\n+**Likelihood:** LOW\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     `uwsgi.ini` line 6 (`processes = 5`), no `--harakiri`/`--request-timeout`.\n+Transform:  A slow `urlopen` (profile_image SSRF, utils/profile_image.py:7) blocks one worker indefinitely; with only 5 workers, 5 slow requests exhaust all.\n+Sink:       uwsgi rejects further requests (503) — DoS.\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n+**Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n+**Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`).\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","patch":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -373,4 +373,21 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker triggers a resource-exhaustion / crash path (e.g., large profile_image SSRF fetch, or repeated failures) → 2. no memory/CPU limits → DoS of the host or sibling containers → 3. no restart policy → manual recovery required.\n **Mitigations:** None.\n **Fix:** Add `deploy.resources.limits` (memory/cpus), `restart: unless-stopped`, and `security_opt: [seccomp=default, apparmor=default]` (or `no-new-privileges`).\n+\n+### uwsgi.ini — no request timeout (worker-exhaustion DoS)\n+**CWE:** CWE-400\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** LOW\n+**Likelihood:** LOW\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     `uwsgi.ini` line 6 (`processes = 5`), no `--harakiri`/`--request-timeout`.\n+Transform:  A slow `urlopen` (profile_image SSRF, utils/profile_image.py:7) blocks one worker indefinitely; with only 5 workers, 5 slow requests exhaust all.\n+Sink:       uwsgi rejects further requests (503) — DoS.\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n+**Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n+**Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`).\n","additions":17,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":".security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","time":{"start":1788193626007,"end":1788193626012}},"id":"prt_058a55782001yBsBvFMy3eSRFm","sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","messageID":"msg_058a4e6d3001r4wvOaXToQ5UJS"}}
