{"type":"text","timestamp":1788193659347,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"id":"prt_058a5a573001b2uSg4O2WLGfvo","messageID":"msg_058a56dc50019rnEroHKjkzFg5","sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","type":"text","text":"\n\n`conf/nginx.conf` — listens on HTTP port 80 with no HTTPS redirect, no HSTS, no security headers, no `server_tokens off`. Main finding: session cookies/auth tokens transmitted in plaintext (MITM). Recorded:\n\n","time":{"start":1788193645939,"end":1788193659344}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788193659359,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_509b358b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","oldString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n**Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n**Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`).","newString":"**Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n**Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n**Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`).\n\n### conf/nginx.conf:27-28 — HTTP-only, no HTTPS / HSTS (session interception)\n**CWE:** CWE-319 (cleartext transmission) — reported under the allowed CWE list as CWE-200\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** MODERATE\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `nginx.conf` lines 27-28 — `listen 80` / `listen [::]:80` (HTTP only).\nTransform:  No `server_name` HTTPS redirect, no `Strict-Transport-Security` header, no `server_tokens off;`, no security headers (X-Frame-Options / X-Content-Type-Options / CSP).\nSink:       All requests — including signed session cookies (signed with the hardcoded `app.secret_key`) and the `preferences`/`remember_token` cookies — traverse the network in plaintext.\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker on the same network (MITM / ARP spoofing / rogue Wi-Fi) captures the plaintext response → 2. reads the signed session cookie / `remember_token` → 3. replays the session (auth state hijack).\n**Mitigations:** None (HTTP-only, no HSTS, no security headers, version exposed via `server_tokens`).\n**Fix:** Terminate TLS at nginx (or a reverse proxy), add `return 301 https://$host$request_uri;`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, and `server_tokens off;`."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -390,4 +390,21 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n **Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n **Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`).\n+\n+### conf/nginx.conf:27-28 — HTTP-only, no HTTPS / HSTS (session interception)\n+**CWE:** CWE-319 (cleartext transmission) — reported under the allowed CWE list as CWE-200\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** MODERATE\n+**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     `nginx.conf` lines 27-28 — `listen 80` / `listen [::]:80` (HTTP only).\n+Transform:  No `server_name` HTTPS redirect, no `Strict-Transport-Security` header, no `server_tokens off;`, no security headers (X-Frame-Options / X-Content-Type-Options / CSP).\n+Sink:       All requests — including signed session cookies (signed with the hardcoded `app.secret_key`) and the `preferences`/`remember_token` cookies — traverse the network in plaintext.\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker on the same network (MITM / ARP spoofing / rogue Wi-Fi) captures the plaintext response → 2. reads the signed session cookie / `remember_token` → 3. replays the session (auth state hijack).\n+**Mitigations:** None (HTTP-only, no HSTS, no security headers, version exposed via `server_tokens`).\n+**Fix:** Terminate TLS at nginx (or a reverse proxy), add `return 301 https://$host$request_uri;`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, and `server_tokens off;`.\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","patch":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -390,4 +390,21 @@\n \n **Exploit:** 1. Attacker submits 5+ profile images with slow/lingering URLs → 2. each worker blocks on `urlopen` → 3. app stops responding.\n **Mitigations:** None (no harakiri/request timeout). Partial — uwsgi drops privileges to `www-data` (lines 3-4), which partially mitigates the Dockerfile root finding.\n **Fix:** Add `harakiri = 30` (or `--request-timeout`), and worker-recycling (`max-requests`).\n+\n+### conf/nginx.conf:27-28 — HTTP-only, no HTTPS / HSTS (session interception)\n+**CWE:** CWE-319 (cleartext transmission) — reported under the allowed CWE list as CWE-200\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** MODERATE\n+**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n+\n+**Data flow:**\n+Source:     `nginx.conf` lines 27-28 — `listen 80` / `listen [::]:80` (HTTP only).\n+Transform:  No `server_name` HTTPS redirect, no `Strict-Transport-Security` header, no `server_tokens off;`, no security headers (X-Frame-Options / X-Content-Type-Options / CSP).\n+Sink:       All requests — including signed session cookies (signed with the hardcoded `app.secret_key`) and the `preferences`/`remember_token` cookies — traverse the network in plaintext.\n+\n+**Exploit:** 1. Attacker on the same network (MITM / ARP spoofing / rogue Wi-Fi) captures the plaintext response → 2. reads the signed session cookie / `remember_token` → 3. replays the session (auth state hijack).\n+**Mitigations:** None (HTTP-only, no HSTS, no security headers, version exposed via `server_tokens`).\n+**Fix:** Terminate TLS at nginx (or a reverse proxy), add `return 301 https://$host$request_uri;`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, and `server_tokens off;`.\n","additions":17,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":".security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","time":{"start":1788193659352,"end":1788193659356}},"id":"prt_058a5d9bc001AyG3dWCEGtAYXi","sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","messageID":"msg_058a56dc50019rnEroHKjkzFg5"}}
