{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788193902093,"sessionID":"ses_fa773389fffevh97Nl5ZXjkxvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_0d786536","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Security Assessment — 2026-08-31 — Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit\n2: \n3: ## Context\n4: **Project:** Extremely Vulnerable Flask App — intentionally vulnerable Flask app for educational purposes\n5: **Language/framework:** Python 3.x / Flask (SQLAlchemy + SQLite, Jinja templating, Bootstrap-Flask)\n6: **Purpose:** Educational demonstration of web application vulnerabilities; invite-based registration with normal vs admin users.\n7: **Deployment:** Docker container — uwsgi (5 processes) behind nginx, published HTTP :5000 → container :80\n8: **Ports/services:** HTTP :5000 (→80); SQLite file `database.db`; uwsgi socket `/tmp/uwsgi.socket` (chmod 664)\n9: **Auth model:** Invite-based registration (hardcoded leaked invite code in README); predefined `admin@evfa.com:admin` — exact model confirmed in routes (see Attack surface)\n10: **Data stores:** SQLite via SQLAlchemy (`database.db`)\n11: **External integrations:** none visible\n12: **Notes:** Leaked invite code + hardcoded admin credentials published in README; Dockerfile installs nginx + build-essential + python3-dev (large attack surface); uwsgi socket world-writable (664); no explicit `USER` in Dockerfile (uwsgi drops privileges to www-data via ini).\n13: \n14: ### graphify-out status\n15: graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md not available (graph.json present but not read per instructions). Attack-path / dead-code analysis (step 4b) skipped — no GRAPH_REPORT.md.\n16: \n17: ## Semgrep baseline\n18: 8 findings (ERROR/WARNING), concentrated in account.py, app.py, profile_image.py:\n19: | account.py:33 | avoid-sqlalchemy-text (CWE-89 SQLi) | ERROR |\n20: | account.py:105 | insecure-deserialization (CWE-502 pickle) | ERROR |\n21: | account.py:105 | secure-set-cookie (CWE-614) | WARNING |\n22: | account.py:105 | avoid-pickle (CWE-502) | WARNING |\n23: | account.py:118 | avoid-pickle (CWE-502) | WARNING |\n24: | account.py:128 | avoid-pickle (CWE-502) | WARNING |\n25: | app.py:31 | render-template-string / SSTI (CWE-96) | WARNING |\n26: | profile_image.py:7 | dynamic-urllib-use / SSRF-ish (CWE-939) | WARNING |\n27: \n28: ## Secret scan baseline\n29: TruffleHog: no secrets found (0 candidates) (trufflehog-results.json empty, 3 bytes).\n30: \n31: ## Dependency scan baseline\n32: Grype (2) + OSV-Scanner (3; click only surfaced via OSV):\n33: | package | version | CVE/SEC | severity | fixed-in |\n34: |---|---|---|---|---|\n35: | click | 8.1.7 | PYSEC-2026-2132 (command injection) | High (7.2) | 8.3.3 |\n36: | flask | 3.1.1 | CVE-2026-27205 (Vary: Cookie header) | Low (4.3) | 3.1.3 |\n37: | flask | 3.1.1 | PYSEC-2026-2151 | Medium (4.3) | 3.1.3 |\n38: | werkzeug | 3.1.5 | CVE-2026-27199 (safe_join Windows device names) | Medium (5.3) | 3.1.6 |\n39: | werkzeug | 3.1.5 | PYSEC-2026-2320 | Medium (6.3) | 3.1.6 |\n40: \n41: Note: SBOM available (`sbom.cyclonedx.json`) — used in step 7.\n42: \n43: ## Attack surface\n44: ### Entry points\n45: | # | Type | Location | Auth required | Description |\n46: |---|---|---|---|---|\n47: | 1 | WSGI entry | app.py:1 | n/a | Flask app factory (`app = Flask(...)`) |\n48: | 2 | Auth redirect | app.py:24 | no | `unauthorized_handler` → login redirect |\n49: | 3 | HTTP route | routes/home.py:8,14 | login | home page |\n50: | 4 | HTTP route | routes/login.py:17-22 | no | login GET/POST (`hashpw` verify) |\n51: | 5 | HTTP route | routes/signup.py:33 | invite code | signup POST (`validate_token`) |\n52: | 6 | HTTP route | routes/account.py:18 /account | login | profile view |\n53: | 7 | HTTP route | routes/account.py:24 /search | login | search → `text()` SQLi (account.py:33) |\n54: | 8 | HTTP route | routes/account.py:51 /account/image POST | login | image upload → urllib (profile_image.py:7) |\n55: | 9 | HTTP route | routes/account.py:68 /account POST | login | account update → `__dict__.update` mass-assign + pickle (105/118/128) |\n56: | 10 | HTTP route | routes/account.py:98 /darkmode POST | login | theme toggle |\n57: | 11 | HTTP route | routes/registration_codes.py:26 /registration-codes POST | admin | generate registration code |\n58: | 12 | HTTP route | routes/notes.py:16 /notes POST | login | create note |\n59: | 13 | HTTP route | routes/notes.py:39 /notes/<int:note_id>/delete POST | login | delete note (IDOR risk) |\n60: | 14 | CLI | db_seed.py | n/a | DB seed script (creates users/notes) |\n61: \n62: ### Trust boundaries\n63: | # | Boundary | Location | Data type |\n64: |---|---|---|---|\n65: | 1 | Unauth→Auth | routes/*.py `@login_required` | session/credentials |\n66: | 2 | Auth→Admin | routes/registration_codes.py:15,29 (`current_user.is_admin`) | admin flag |\n67: | 3 | Web input→SQL | routes/account.py:33, signup.py:16 (`text(f\"...\")`) | SQL query |\n68: | 4 | Web input→pickle | routes/account.py:105,118,128 | serialized object |\n69: | 5 | Web input→template | app.py:31 (`render_template_string`) | HTML template |\n70: | 6 | File upload→network | utils/profile_image.py:7 (`urllib`) | external URL |\n71: | 7 | Form→ORM model | routes/account.py:81 (`__dict__.update`) | mass assignment |\n72: \n73: ### Notes\n74: - `forms/account_form.py:8` exposes `is_admin` BooleanField; `routes/account.py:81` mass-updates `current_user.__dict__` from form fields → privilege-escalation / mass-attack surface (admin field reachable by any logged-in user).\n75: - Registration invite code hardcoded and published in README (`a36e990b-...`); predefined `admin@evfa.com:admin` credentials in README.\n76: - uwsgi socket `chmod-sock = 664` (world-writable